p7_desc":"How consistency, support, and the right plan made the difference.","p8_category":"EVENTS & HIGHLIGHTS","p8_title":"Sunrise Stretch & Recover at Sala Park","p8_desc":"A refreshing morning of movement and connection."},"why_title":"Why we share","why_desc":"We believe better movement comes from better information and real experiences. Our goal is to build trust through transparency, share practical insights you can use, and grow a community that moves, recovers, and lives better — together.","why_f1_title":"Evidence-informed insights","why_f1_desc":"Knowledge you can trust and apply.","why_f2_title":"Real stories from real people","why_f2_desc":"Experiences that inspire and connect.","why_f3_title":"Practical takeaways for everyday life","why_f3_desc":"Simple steps for lasting impact.","cta_title":"Explore more. Move better. Live better.","cta_subtitle":"Discover our services, book a session, or follow us for the latest updates.","cta_explore":"Explore Our Services","cta_book":"Book a Session","cta_follow":"Follow Updates","detail":{"back_to_hub":"Back to Sharing Hub","on_this_page":"On this page","categories":"Categories","tags":"Tags","related_posts":"You may also want to read","view_all_articles":"View all articles","by":"By","min_read":"min read","sidebar_cta_title":"Looking for support with your recovery or performance?","sidebar_cta_desc":"Our team is here to help you move better and feel your best.","sidebar_cta_btn":"Book a Session","sidebar_business_title":"Business Solution for Your Organization","sidebar_business_desc":"Professional recovery solutions for teams, events & workplaces.","sidebar_business_btn":"Explore for Business","what_is_sport_recovery":{"title":"What Is Sport Recovery and Why It Matters for Everyone Who Moves","excerpt":"Sport recovery is more than rest. It's a structured process that helps your body adapt, reduce pain, and perform better. Here's what you need to know.","intro":{"title":"What is sport recovery?","text":"Sport recovery is the intentional process of helping your body return to balance after physical stress. It supports muscle tissue repair, reduces soreness, and prepares you for your next training or competition.","quote":"Recovery is where progress happens. Without it, performance doesn't last."},"why":{"title":"Why it matters","text":"Good recovery helps you:","b1":"Reduce muscle soreness and fatigue","b2":"Lower risk of injury","b3":"Improve mobility and movement quality","b4":"Perform at your best, more consistently"},"components":{"title":"The key components of sport recovery","c1":{"title":"Movement Restoration","desc":"Improve mobility and restore range of motion"},"c2":{"title":"Soft Tissue Work","desc":"Release tension and reduce muscle tightness"},"c3":{"title":"Recovery Modalities","desc":"Use the right tools to speed up recovery"},"c4":{"title":"Hydration & Nutrition","desc":"Fuel your body to repair and perform"},"c5":{"title":"Sleep & Rest","desc":"Quality rest is where your body adapts and grows"}},"who":{"title":"Who can benefit?","text":"Anyone who moves. From athletes to weekend warriors to people with desk jobs, sport recovery can help you move better, feel better, and stay consistent."},"start":{"title":"How to get started","text":"Start with understanding your body. Listen to the signs. Then, build a simple recovery routine that works for you. Need help? Our team is here to support you."},"takeaways":{"title":"Key takeaways","text":"Recovery is a journey, not a destination. Listen to your body, stay consistent, and don't hesitate to seek professional guidance when needed."}},"foam_rolling_101":{"title":"Foam Rolling 101: Simple Habits for Better Recovery","excerpt":"Discover how foam rolling can reduce muscle tension, improve mobility, and support your daily recovery routine — no gym required.","intro":{"title":"What is foam rolling?","text":"Foam rolling is a self-myofascial release (SMR) technique that uses your own body weight to apply targeted pressure to tight or sore muscles. By slowly rolling over a foam cylinder, you help break up adhesions in the fascia — the connective tissue surrounding your muscles — improving blood flow, reducing stiffness, and promoting faster recovery. Unlike deep tissue massage, foam rolling puts you in control of the intensity and allows you to target specific areas on your own schedule.","quote":"The best recovery tool is the one you actually use. Foam rolling takes five minutes, costs almost nothing, and can change how your body feels every day."},"why":{"title":"Why foam rolling works","text":"Foam rolling works by stimulating blood circulation and releasing fascial tension that builds up from exercise, prolonged sitting, or repetitive movement patterns. Research shows that regular foam rolling can:","b1":"Reduce delayed-onset muscle soreness (DOMS) after exercise by up to 30%","b2":"Increase joint range of motion without decreasing muscle strength","b3":"Improve blood flow to fatigued muscles, accelerating nutrient delivery","b4":"Lower perceived fatigue and improve recovery between training sessions"},"technique":{"title":"How to foam roll effectively","text":"Start by placing the foam roller under the target muscle group. Use your body weight to apply moderate pressure and slowly roll back and forth for 30 to 60 seconds per area. When you find a particularly tight or tender spot — a trigger point — pause and hold pressure there for 20 to 30 seconds. Breathe deeply and allow the tissue to release naturally. Avoid rolling directly over joints or bones. Focus on major muscle groups: calves, quadriceps, hamstrings, glutes, upper back, and the IT band. For beginners, a softer foam roller is recommended. As your tolerance builds, you can progress to denser rollers for deeper tissue work."},"mistakes":{"title":"Common mistakes to avoid","text":"Many people roll too quickly, which reduces the effectiveness of the technique. Slow, controlled movements are far more beneficial than fast passes. Another common mistake is applying too much pressure on sensitive areas — if it's painful rather than uncomfortable, ease off. Avoid foam rolling your lower back directly, as this can compress the spine; instead, use a lacrosse ball or target the muscles on either side. Finally, don't skip the warm-up: a few minutes of light movement before foam rolling helps increase tissue temperature and makes the process more effective."},"routine":{"title":"Building your foam rolling routine","text":"Consistency is more important than duration. A simple 5-to-10-minute foam rolling routine before or after exercise can make a significant difference over time. For best results, foam roll after your workout to reduce soreness and before bed to promote relaxation. You can also use foam rolling as a standalone recovery session on rest days. The key is to listen to your body, stay patient, and make it a habit. If you're unsure where to start or want guidance tailored to your activity level, our team at Stretch.vn can help you build a personalized recovery plan."}},"hip_mobility_key":{"title":"Hip Mobility: The Key to Stronger, Pain-Free Movement","excerpt":"Tight hips affect everything from your posture to your performance. Learn simple assessments and exercises to unlock better, pain-free movement.","intro":{"title":"Why hip mobility matters","text":"Your hips are the central hub of your body's movement system. They connect your upper body to your lower body, bear your full weight during walking and running, and provide the foundation for nearly every athletic movement. When hip mobility is limited, your body compensates — often leading to lower back pain, knee discomfort, poor posture, and reduced performance. Whether you sit at a desk all day, run regularly, or play sports on weekends, investing in hip mobility is one of the most impactful things you can do for your body.","quote":"Your hips don't lie — and neither does restricted movement. Unlock your hips, and you unlock your potential."},"signs":{"title":"Signs your hips need attention","text":"Your body sends clear signals when hip mobility is becoming an issue. Paying attention to these signs early can prevent more serious problems down the road:","b1":"Persistent tightness or stiffness in the front of your hips after sitting","b2":"Lower back pain that worsens with prolonged standing or walking","b3":"Difficulty squatting deeply or performing lunges with proper form","b4":"Knee pain or tracking issues during running or climbing stairs"},"assessment":{"title":"Simple hip mobility assessments","text":"You don't need expensive equipment to assess your hip mobility. Try the deep squat test: stand with feet shoulder-width apart and slowly lower into a full squat. If your heels lift, your knees cave inward, or you can't maintain an upright torso, your hips likely need work. The Thomas test is another quick check: lie on your back at the edge of a table, pull one knee to your chest, and let the other leg hang. If the hanging leg lifts off the table or the knee can't bend to 90 degrees, hip flexor tightness is present. These simple screenings can give you valuable insight into where your limitations are."},"exercises":{"title":"Exercises to improve hip mobility","text":"Start with controlled movements that gradually increase range of motion. The 90/90 stretch — sitting with both legs at 90-degree angles — opens both internal and external rotation. Hip circles in a tabletop position warm up the joint capsule and improve fluidity. Pigeon pose targets the deep external rotators and hip flexors simultaneously. For strength-based mobility, goblet squats with a pause at the bottom and lateral lunges build both range and control. Aim for 10 to 15 minutes of focused hip work three to four times per week. Consistency matters more than intensity — small daily improvements compound into lasting change."},"routine":{"title":"Making hip mobility part of your routine","text":"The best hip mobility routine is one you can sustain. Integrate 5 minutes of hip work into your warm-up before exercise and 5 minutes of stretching into your cool-down. On rest days, a dedicated 15-minute mobility session can accelerate progress significantly. If you experience persistent pain or significant limitation, a professional assessment can identify specific restrictions and create a targeted plan. At Stretch.vn, our team specializes in movement assessment and personalized recovery plans that address the root cause — not just the symptoms."}},"new_chapter_stretch":{"title":"A New Chapter for Stretch.vn","excerpt":"From our roots in sport recovery to a full movement health ecosystem — here's what's been happening and what's coming next for Stretch.vn.","intro":{"title":"Where we started","text":"Stretch.vn began with a simple idea: bring professional-quality recovery to people who move. We started at running events, setting up recovery stations for tired runners who needed more than just water and a banana. Those early days taught us something important — recovery isn't a luxury, it's a necessity. And the people who need it most often have the least access to it. That insight shaped everything we've built since.","quote":"We didn't set out to build a company. We set out to solve a problem. The company grew because the problem was bigger than we thought."},"changed":{"title":"What's changed","text":"In the past year, Stretch.vn has evolved from a focused event recovery service into a comprehensive movement health platform. We've expanded our team with qualified therapists and movement specialists, opened a dedicated clinic space, and developed structured programs for both individuals and organizations. Our corporate wellness program now serves multiple companies across Ho Chi Minh City, and our education track has trained dozens of practitioners in evidence-based recovery techniques. But the biggest change isn't in what we do — it's in how we think. We now approach every interaction with a systems mindset, looking at the whole person rather than isolated symptoms."},"learned":{"title":"What we've learned","text":"Building Stretch.vn has taught us that people don't just want treatment — they want understanding. They want someone who listens before they touch. They want explanations that make sense, not jargon. They want to feel empowered, not dependent. These lessons have fundamentally shaped our approach: we assess before we treat, we educate as we work, and we give every client something they can take home and apply on their own. Recovery isn't something that happens to you — it's something you learn to do for yourself, with the right support."},"next":{"title":"What's next for Stretch.vn","text":"Looking ahead, we're focused on three priorities. First, making quality recovery more accessible — through flexible scheduling, home visits, and partnerships with community organizations. Second, raising the standard of practitioner training — because better-trained hands mean better outcomes for everyone. Third, building a knowledge platform that helps people understand their bodies and make informed decisions about their care. This Sharing Hub is part of that vision. We believe that when people understand how their body works, they take better care of it. And that's good for everyone."}},"new_space_thao_dien":{"title":"Our New Space in Thao Dien is Now Open","excerpt":"A space designed for focused care, better movement, and meaningful connections. Come see what we've built for you in Thao Dien.","intro":{"title":"A space built with purpose","text":"After months of planning and preparation, we're excited to announce that our new recovery and movement space in Thao Dien is officially open. This isn't just a new address — it's a reflection of everything we believe recovery should be. Every detail has been designed with care: from the treatment rooms that allow for focused, uninterrupted sessions, to the open movement area where clients can learn exercises and stretches they'll take home. The space is warm, professional, and intentionally minimal — because recovery works best when there's nothing in the way.","quote":"A good space doesn't just look good. It makes the work better. That's what we built."},"find":{"title":"What you'll find here","text":"The Thao Dien space features private treatment rooms equipped for hands-on therapy and assessment, a movement education zone for guided exercises and workshops, and a welcoming reception area where you can discuss your needs before your session. We've invested in quality treatment tables, mobility tools, and rehabilitation equipment that support a wide range of recovery and movement work. The space also includes a consultation area for longer assessments and program planning, making it ideal for both first-time visitors and long-term clients."},"designed":{"title":"Designed for your recovery","text":"Our design philosophy was simple: remove friction. We wanted a space where you can arrive, feel comfortable immediately, and focus entirely on your recovery. Natural light fills the treatment rooms. Noise is minimal. The temperature is controlled for comfort during sessions. We chose materials that are clean, durable, and easy to maintain — because hygiene and professionalism are non-negotiable in recovery care. Whether you're coming for a post-run stretch, a rehabilitation session, or a movement assessment, this space was built to support you at every stage."},"visit":{"title":"Visit us","text":"Our Thao Dien space is open Monday through Saturday, with both morning and afternoon sessions available. We recommend booking in advance to secure your preferred time slot, though walk-ins are welcome when availability allows. If you're new to Stretch.vn, your first visit will include a brief assessment to help us understand your body, your goals, and how we can best support you. Come see the space, meet the team, and experience recovery that's built around you."}},"growing_team_elevating_care":{"title":"Growing the Team, Elevating Care","excerpt":"Welcoming new therapists and coaches to the Stretch.vn family. Meet the people who are raising the standard of recovery care.","intro":{"title":"Why we're growing","text":"Demand for quality recovery support has grown significantly over the past year. More runners, athletes, office workers, and active adults are seeking professional help with their movement and recovery. To meet this demand without compromising quality, we've expanded our team with carefully selected therapists and coaches who share our values and commitment to excellence. Every new team member goes through an extensive onboarding process that includes clinical skills assessment, communication training, and supervised practice before they work independently.","quote":"Growing isn't about getting bigger. It's about getting better — with more hands, more perspectives, and more capacity to help."},"philosophy":{"title":"Our hiring philosophy","text":"We don't hire based on credentials alone. While clinical qualifications are essential, we look for people who combine technical skill with genuine empathy and curiosity. Our ideal team member asks questions, listens deeply, and is always learning. They understand that recovery is a relationship, not a transaction. During our hiring process, we assess hands-on skills, communication ability, and adaptability to different client needs. We also look for cultural fit — because the best care happens when the team works well together and supports each other's growth."},"means":{"title":"What this means for you","text":"More team members mean more availability, shorter wait times, and greater flexibility in scheduling. It also means deeper specialization — with new practitioners bringing expertise in areas like sports-specific recovery, post-surgical rehabilitation, and workplace ergonomics. We've also strengthened our supervision structure, with senior therapists mentoring newer team members to ensure consistency across every session. Whether you see our most experienced practitioner or our newest team member, you can expect the same standard of assessment, treatment, and care."},"ahead":{"title":"The road ahead","text":"Our growth is far from finished. We're continuing to invest in our team's professional development through regular training sessions, external workshops, and collaborative case reviews. We believe that a well-supported, well-trained team delivers better outcomes — and that's ultimately what matters. If you're a therapist or movement professional who shares our values, we'd love to hear from you. And if you're a client, we invite you to experience the difference that a growing, dedicated team can make in your recovery journey."}},"meet_huy_team_story":{"title":"Meet Huy: Driven by Curiosity, Guided by Purpose","excerpt":"From sports science student to recovery specialist — Huy shares his journey, his philosophy, and what drives him to help people move better every day.","intro":{"title":"The beginning","text":"Huy's journey into recovery work didn't start in a clinic — it started on the field. As a university student studying sports science, he was fascinated by the gap between how athletes trained and how they recovered. He saw teammates push through pain, ignore warning signs, and end up with injuries that could have been prevented. That frustration led him to dive deeper into the science of recovery, movement assessment, and rehabilitation. After graduating, he joined Stretch.vn — and found a team that shared his belief that recovery should be proactive, not reactive.","quote":"I didn't choose recovery work. It chose me. Every time I see someone move better after a session, I know I'm exactly where I'm supposed to be."},"path":{"title":"Finding his path","text":"Before joining Stretch.vn, Huy worked with amateur football teams and running groups, providing basic recovery support at events and training sessions. Those experiences taught him something that textbooks couldn't: every body tells a different story. A runner's tight calves might stem from hip weakness. An office worker's neck pain might be connected to breathing patterns. These connections fascinated Huy and pushed him to pursue deeper education in functional movement assessment and manual therapy. At Stretch.vn, he found a structured environment where he could apply this systems-thinking approach with real clients every day."},"approach":{"title":"His approach to recovery","text":"Huy's sessions always start with listening. Before he touches a muscle, he wants to understand your daily routine, your training habits, your pain history, and your goals. This comprehensive intake allows him to create a session plan that addresses root causes rather than just symptoms. His hands-on work combines stretching, soft tissue techniques, and movement re-education — always explaining what he's doing and why. Clients consistently describe his sessions as both educational and therapeutic. Huy believes that a good session should leave you not just feeling better, but understanding your body better."},"drives":{"title":"What drives him every day","text":"Ask Huy what motivates him, and his answer is simple: progress. Not the dramatic, overnight kind — but the small, meaningful improvements that compound over weeks and months. A client who can finally squat without pain. A runner who finishes a race without cramping. An office worker who sleeps better because their shoulder tension is resolved. These moments remind Huy why he does this work. Outside of sessions, he's constantly reading research papers, attending workshops, and exchanging ideas with the Stretch.vn team. For Huy, learning never stops — and neither does the drive to help people move better."}},"behind_session_listening":{"title":"Behind the Session: The Power of Listening","excerpt":"The most effective recovery starts before any technique is applied. It starts with truly understanding your story, your body, and your goals.","intro":{"title":"More than technique","text":"Walk into most recovery or therapy sessions, and the process feels familiar: lie down, describe where it hurts, receive treatment, leave. At Stretch.vn, we've built our entire approach around a different starting point — listening. Not the polite, nodding-along kind of listening, but the deep, investigative kind that connects what you feel with why you feel it. We've found that when practitioners truly listen, they discover patterns and connections that change the entire course of treatment. A shoulder problem might actually stem from how you breathe. Knee pain might be related to ankle mobility you lost years ago. These connections only surface when someone takes the time to ask the right questions and listen to the answers.","quote":"The body doesn't speak in diagnoses. It speaks in movement patterns, compensation, and pain signals. Our job is to translate."},"why_listen":{"title":"Why we listen first","text":"In clinical practice, the assessment is often the most valuable part of a session. It tells the practitioner not just what to treat, but how to treat it, how aggressively to work, and what to avoid. A client who's been dealing with chronic lower back pain for five years needs a fundamentally different approach than someone who tweaked their back yesterday. By listening first — to your history, your habits, your goals, and your concerns — we can design a session that's truly tailored to you. We've seen time and again that sessions guided by deep understanding produce faster, more lasting results than sessions guided by assumption."},"reveals":{"title":"What listening reveals","text":"Every person carries a unique movement history. Your sport, your job, your injuries, your stress levels, even your sleep quality — all of these shape how your body moves and where it holds tension. Through careful conversation and observation, our practitioners identify patterns that would be invisible to someone who just focuses on the painful spot. We've discovered hip restrictions caused by years of driving. Shoulder tension rooted in work-related stress. Knee issues connected to an old ankle sprain that never fully healed. These revelations don't just change the session — they change the client's understanding of their own body."},"experience":{"title":"How this changes your experience","text":"When you feel truly heard, the entire recovery experience changes. Trust builds faster. You share more openly. You follow home exercises more consistently because you understand why they matter. At Stretch.vn, we've built our intake process, our session structure, and our follow-up protocols around the principle of active listening. It's not always the fastest approach — but it's the most effective one. Because at the end of the day, we're not just treating muscles. We're partnering with people who want to understand and take care of their bodies. And that partnership starts with listening."}},"setbacks_to_strength_kevin":{"title":"From Setbacks to Strength: Kevin's Journey","excerpt":"After a knee injury threatened to end his active lifestyle, Kevin found a path back through consistent recovery, patience, and the right support system.","intro":{"title":"The moment everything changed","text":"Kevin had always been active. Running three times a week, playing weekend football, hitting the gym — movement was a core part of his identity. Then, during a casual football match, a sudden change of direction sent a sharp pain through his right knee. The diagnosis: a meniscus tear that would require surgery and months of careful rehabilitation. For someone who defined himself through physical activity, the injury wasn't just physical — it was emotional. Kevin felt lost, frustrated, and unsure if he'd ever return to the activities he loved.","quote":"The hardest part wasn't the surgery. It was the morning after, when I realized I couldn't do the things I'd always taken for granted."},"process":{"title":"The recovery process","text":"Kevin's rehabilitation journey began with small, deliberate steps. In the early weeks post-surgery, the focus was on reducing swelling, restoring basic range of motion, and managing pain. Working with the Stretch.vn team, Kevin followed a structured recovery plan that progressed from gentle stretching and mobility work to more demanding strengthening exercises. Each week brought measurable improvements — a few more degrees of knee flexion, a few more steps without support, a little more confidence. The process was slow, often frustrating, but Kevin stayed committed because he could see and feel the progress."},"difference":{"title":"What made the difference","text":"Looking back, Kevin identifies three factors that made his recovery successful. First, having a clear plan with milestones gave him something to work toward every week. Second, the combination of professional treatment and home exercises created a recovery rhythm that kept his body adapting between sessions. Third — and this surprised him most — the emotional support mattered just as much as the physical work. His practitioners didn't just treat his knee; they acknowledged his frustration, celebrated his progress, and adjusted the plan when setbacks occurred. This holistic approach kept Kevin engaged and motivated throughout the process."},"now":{"title":"Where Kevin is now","text":"Six months after his surgery, Kevin is back to running — not at his previous pace, but with better form and a much deeper understanding of how his body works. He's incorporated regular mobility work into his routine, something he never prioritized before. He still visits Stretch.vn periodically for maintenance sessions and movement check-ups. Most importantly, his relationship with exercise has changed. He no longer pushes through pain or ignores warning signs. He listens to his body, respects its limits, and invests in recovery as seriously as he invests in training. Kevin's story is a reminder that setbacks don't have to be endings — they can be the beginning of a stronger, smarter approach to movement."}},"recovery_day_vn_runners":{"title":"Recovery Day with VN Runners Club","excerpt":"Over 120 runners joined us for a day of movement screening, recovery sessions, and community. Here's what happened and what we learned together.","intro":{"title":"A day of recovery","text":"On a warm Saturday morning in Ho Chi Minh City, Stretch.vn partnered with VN Runners Club for a dedicated Recovery Day — an event designed to show runners that taking care of their bodies is just as important as logging miles. Over 120 runners showed up, many of them training for upcoming marathons and half-marathons. The energy was incredible: a mix of curiosity, community spirit, and genuine eagerness to learn. For many participants, this was their first experience with professional recovery support, and the feedback was overwhelmingly positive.","quote":"Runners are incredibly disciplined about their training. We wanted to show them that recovery deserves the same discipline."},"what_we_did":{"title":"What we did","text":"The Recovery Day featured three main components. First, a movement screening station where our practitioners conducted brief assessments — checking hip mobility, ankle range of motion, and single-leg balance. Second, recovery treatment stations offering targeted stretching, soft tissue work, and foam rolling guidance. Third, an education area with short talks on topics like post-run recovery nutrition, the importance of sleep, and how to recognize early signs of overuse injuries. Each runner received a personalized recovery card with their assessment results and recommended exercises to work on before their next race."},"learned":{"title":"What runners learned","text":"The movement screenings revealed some eye-opening patterns. Over 60% of participants had significant limitations in hip internal rotation — a common finding among runners that can contribute to IT band syndrome and knee pain. Nearly half showed restricted ankle dorsiflexion, which affects running mechanics and increases load on the knees and calves. Most runners were surprised by these findings because they didn't experience pain — yet. This is exactly why screening matters: it catches potential problems before they become injuries. Many participants left with a new appreciation for the role mobility plays in running performance and longevity."},"community":{"title":"Community in action","text":"Beyond the clinical value, Recovery Day was a celebration of community. Runners shared stories, compared assessment results, and encouraged each other to take recovery more seriously. We saw experienced ultramarathoners learning from our practitioners alongside first-time 5K runners. The common thread was clear: everyone wanted to keep running, and they were willing to invest in the work that makes that possible. Events like this remind us why Stretch.vn exists — not just to treat problems, but to build a culture where taking care of your body is a normal, valued part of an active life. We're already planning the next one."}},"movement_workshop_rmit":{"title":"Movement Workshop at RMIT Vietnam","excerpt":"Great energy and thoughtful questions from students eager to understand their bodies. A recap of our educational workshop at RMIT Vietnam.","intro":{"title":"Bringing movement education to campus","text":"When RMIT Vietnam invited Stretch.vn to conduct a movement and recovery workshop for their student community, we jumped at the opportunity. University students represent a unique population: they're generally young and active, but they're also sitting in lectures for hours, carrying heavy bags, studying under pressure, and often neglecting basic physical care. Our goal was simple — give them practical tools they could use immediately to feel better and move more efficiently, without requiring any special equipment or gym membership.","quote":"You don't need to be an athlete to benefit from movement education. You just need a body — and everyone qualifies."},"covered":{"title":"What we covered","text":"The 90-minute workshop was structured around three themes: Awareness, Movement, and Recovery. In the Awareness segment, we guided students through a simple self-assessment — checking their posture, testing their hip and shoulder mobility, and identifying areas of tension they'd been ignoring. The Movement segment introduced basic mobility exercises that can be done between classes or at a desk: neck circles, thoracic rotations, hip flexor stretches, and ankle mobility drills. The Recovery segment focused on practical techniques like foam rolling, breathing exercises for stress reduction, and simple stretching routines for common problem areas."},"engagement":{"title":"Student engagement","text":"What impressed us most was the quality of questions from students. They asked about the relationship between stress and muscle tension, how sleep affects recovery, whether stretching before exercise actually prevents injury, and how to manage recurring headaches that stem from neck tension. These aren't surface-level questions — they reflect genuine curiosity about how the body works. Several students shared that they'd been dealing with persistent discomfort they assumed was normal: stiff necks from studying, tight shoulders from laptop use, lower back pain from sitting. The workshop helped them realize that these issues are common but not inevitable — and that simple, consistent movement habits can make a real difference."},"forward":{"title":"Looking forward","text":"The RMIT workshop reinforced our belief that movement education should start early. By the time most people seek professional recovery help, they've been dealing with problems for months or years. If we can reach people earlier — in schools, universities, and workplaces — we can help them build habits that prevent problems before they start. We're in discussions with several universities and companies to bring similar workshops to their communities. If your organization is interested in hosting a movement education session, we'd love to hear from you."}},"sunrise_stretch_sala":{"title":"Sunrise Stretch & Recover at Sala Park","excerpt":"A refreshing morning of guided stretching, movement education, and community connection at one of Ho Chi Minh City's most beautiful parks.","intro":{"title":"Morning movement in the park","text":"There's something special about moving your body in the early morning, surrounded by nature, with like-minded people beside you. That's exactly what we set out to create with our Sunrise Stretch & Recover event at Sala Park. Held on a Sunday morning from 6:00 to 8:00 AM, the event brought together over 60 participants of all ages and fitness levels for a guided session of stretching, mobility work, and light movement. The atmosphere was relaxed, the energy was positive, and the sunrise over the park provided the perfect backdrop for a morning of mindful movement.","quote":"Movement doesn't always need to be intense. Sometimes the most powerful thing you can do is slow down, breathe, and stretch."},"session":{"title":"The session","text":"The two-hour event was divided into three segments. We began with a 30-minute guided warm-up that included gentle joint mobilization, dynamic stretching, and breathing exercises. This was followed by a 45-minute mobility flow led by our senior practitioners, incorporating movements from yoga, functional mobility training, and rehabilitation exercises. Participants were guided through hip openers, spinal rotations, shoulder mobility sequences, and balance challenges. The final segment was a 30-minute cool-down with assisted stretching — where our team provided hands-on support to help participants achieve deeper stretches safely and comfortably."},"response":{"title":"Community response","text":"The response exceeded our expectations. Participants ranged from teenagers to retirees, from competitive runners to people who hadn't exercised in months. Many told us it was the first time they'd experienced guided stretching in an outdoor setting, and the combination of fresh air, professional guidance, and community support made the experience uniquely enjoyable. Several participants mentioned that they typically skip stretching entirely — viewing it as boring or unnecessary — but the group format and expert cues made it engaging and accessible. Post-event feedback showed that over 85% of participants wanted to attend future sessions."},"join":{"title":"Join us next time","text":"We plan to host Sunrise Stretch & Recover as a monthly community event, rotating between parks and outdoor spaces across Ho Chi Minh City. These events are open to everyone — no experience needed, no equipment required. We provide mats, guidance, and a welcoming atmosphere. Our goal is to make movement and recovery accessible, enjoyable, and social. If you'd like to join our next session or stay updated on upcoming community events, follow Stretch.vn on social media or reach out to our team directly. Move better. Live better. Together."}}}}},"vi":{"nav":{"home":"Trang chủ","programs":"Chương trình","method":"Phương pháp","studios":"Chi nhánh","membership":"Thẻ thành viên","individual":"Cá nhân","business":"Doanh nghiệp","business_intro":"Giới thiệu","business_recovery":"Phục hồi Y tế tại sự kiện","business_training":"Đào tạo chuyên môn","business_wellness":"Sức Khoẻ doanh nghiệp","blog":"Blog","about":"Về chúng tôi","freeTrial":"Dùng thử miễn phí","bookSession":"Đặt lịch","loginGoogle":"Đăng nhập bằng Google","logout":"Đăng xuất"},"seo":{"home_title":"Stretch.vn — Phục Hồi Vận Động Chuyên Nghiệp","home_desc":"Hỗ trợ phục hồi & vận động cá nhân hóa — tại phòng khám, tại nhà hoặc tại sự kiện của bạn. Đặt lịch online ngay hôm nay.","sharing_hub_title":"Stretch.vn — Góc Chia Sẻ","sharing_hub_desc":"Kiến thức vận động, giáo dục phục hồi, câu chu